# Ignore-matrix interaction with .gitignore (AGENTS.md §6):
#
#   .gitignore                -> what git TRACKS
#   .chezmoiignore (this)     -> what chezmoi APPLIES to the home directory
#
# They are separate decisions, kept in sync manually. Four cases:
#
#   git:ignore + chezmoi:ignore  repo material (docs/, README, node_modules)
#   git:track  + chezmoi:track   real dotfiles (the default; no pattern needed)
#   git:track  + chezmoi:ignore  applied-from-source material that never deploys
#                                here (machine-conditional blocks below)
#   git:ignore + chezmoi:track   FORBIDDEN — chezmoi could not commit the source
#
# docs/check_ignore_consistency.py (CI lint) flags:
#   - a path ignored by one file but negated by the other;
#   - a path both ignored and negated in this file, unless annotated with a
#     `# lint-ok: <family> (<reason>)` comment (used for the gitignore
#     parent-dir un-ignore idiom, e.g. the systemd relay service below).
#
# Machine-conditional entries live inside template if-blocks; the CI
# smoke-apply matrix (augustus/vespasian/unknown/hadrian) validates those
# guards render correctly, so this lint strips the directives and checks the
# pattern set.
#
# One-line bootstrap entry point — repository material, never applied.
dev
install.sh
README.md
AGENTS.md
INDEX.md
INDEX.json
setup.sh
lib
lib/**
.gitignore
.gitleaksignore
.gitleaks.toml
package.json
bun.lock
to-questionnaire-*.md
.github
.github/**

